<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  folio-assistant — the review-log watcher's poll.

  Source of truth: this file. Any SVG of it is generated by `bun run cat
  render:bpmn`; never hand-edit one.

  The mechanical check that decides whether a review log needs agent work: no
  agent work starts unless the sheet or the issues changed. Tool
  review-log-watch; skill review-log-watch.
  Calls contributor-feedback.bpmn for each changed row.
-->
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL"
                  xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC"
                  xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI"
                  xmlns:bootstrap.processes="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/"
                  id="Definitions_ReviewLogWatch"
                  targetNamespace="https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/workflows"
                  exporter="folio-assistant" exporterVersion="1">
  <bpmn:import namespace="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns/" location="https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/processes/ns.jsonld" importType="http://www.w3.org/ns/json-ld"/>
  <bpmn:resource id="authoring-agent" name="Authoring agent"/>

  <bpmn:collaboration id="Collaboration_ReviewLogWatch">
    <bpmn:participant id="Participant_ReviewLogWatch" name="Review-log watch — one poll of one log" processRef="Process_ReviewLogWatch" />
  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="Process_ReviewLogWatch" name="Review-log watch" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>
      One poll of one review log (a drafting Contributor Feedback sheet, or a
      public-comment sheet's Review Change Sets) and its folio repository. A tool decides, with no agent judgement, whether
      anything a person set in the sheet or any open issue changed since the
      last poll. Only then does the agent append rows for new issues and do
      its pass. Skill: review-log-watch.
    </bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="Process_ReviewLogWatch_LaneSet">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_Watcher" name="Log watcher (authoring agent)" partitionElementRef="authoring-agent">
        <bpmn:documentation>The agent thread that watches the log. Until the check says changed it only reads and runs the tool.</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>StartEvent_Poll</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_ReadSheet</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RunCheck</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_StallCheck</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Gateway_Changed</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_AppendRows</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_AgentPass</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_RecordStep</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Task_Accept</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_Done</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>EndEvent_NoWork</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>

    <bpmn:startEvent id="StartEvent_Poll" name="Every minute">
      <bpmn:documentation>The watcher's poll: a chain of 1-minute delayed wakes, each queuing the next before it reads anything, with an hourly scheduled task that restarts the chain if it breaks.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:outgoing>WF01</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:timerEventDefinition id="Timer_Poll"><bpmn:timeCycle>R/PT1M</bpmn:timeCycle></bpmn:timerEventDefinition>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_ReadSheet" name="Read the Contributor Feedback tab">
      <bpmn:documentation>Reads Watch!F1:I1, the hash of the person-set cells that the sheet script writes on every refresh, and Contributor Feedback's header row and Issue column (a public-comment log: Review Change Sets' header row and Change-set column), and saves them as JSON for the check. A sheet without the Watch hash yet is read whole. Reading is not agent work: it changes nothing.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-log-watch"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>WF01</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>WF02</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_RunCheck" name="Run the review-log-watch check">
      <bpmn:documentation>Runs Tool review-log-watch with the folio repository, the saved values and the log's state file. The tool reads the repository's open and closed issues (no pull requests, no issue labelled no-sheet) and compares a digest of them and of the cells people set (Title, Selected Sections, Contributor Feedback, Disposition, Ready for agent, Ready for merge, Dispositions confirmed; on a public-comment log also Committee Feedback, TWG (CS), TWG (human), Change Set (human)) with the last check's. A read with no Issue column tracks only change-set issues and appends no rows, reporting them as issue-unlinked. It writes nothing.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-log-watch"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>WF02</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>WF03</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:task id="Task_StallCheck" name="Hand new feedback to the row's agent; take over stalled rows">
      <bpmn:documentation>On every poll, changed or not, new Blue feedback goes verbatim to the agent working the row, and a stalled row is restarted or taken over. For each row: new Blue feedback goes, verbatim and in the same poll, to the thread that owns the row (named in its Agent row or Feedback (agent)), and Feedback (agent) says who has it. A row is stalled when its Blue cells changed, or Ready for agent turned Yes, more than 10 minutes ago and no Agent step was recorded since; or when its agent recorded no step for 2 hours. A stalled row's owning thread is asked once; with no answer within 10 minutes, or a thread that is done or stopped, the watcher takes the row over, or asks the coordinator for a new thread, and writes the new owner, the step and a link into Feedback (agent).</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-log-watch"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>WF03</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>WF09</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:exclusiveGateway id="Gateway_Changed" name="Sheet or issues changed?">
      <bpmn:documentation>The tool's status. unchanged (exit 0): the poll ends and no other agent work starts. changed (exit 10): its changes and the rows to append go on.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>WF09</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>WF04</bpmn:outgoing>
      <bpmn:outgoing>WF05</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:exclusiveGateway>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_AppendRows" name="Append rows for new issues; hide closed ones">
      <bpmn:documentation>For each row in the tool's append list (one per issue that no row's Issue cell links yet), appends it below the last row of Contributor Feedback: Title is the issue's title, the first Contributor Feedback column @login (#N): the issue's first paragraph, Issue its URL. The script gives each new row its Change-set id. No other writer adds issue rows. Then each row linking a closed issue (the tool's closedRows, and the rows just appended as closed) is hidden and its text struck through.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-log-watch"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>WF04</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>WF06</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_AgentPass" name="Agent pass on the changed rows" calledElement="Process_ContributorFeedback">
      <bpmn:documentation>For each changed row, the agent pass of Contributor feedback on a working draft: Ready for agent = Yes gets its edit, Ready for merge = Yes its merge, and a Blue answer to a Decision needed question is taken up. Every new row (from an issue, a person or a TWG workbook), every row with an empty Feedback (agent) and every row whose Blue cells changed gets feedback in the same wake, in the fixed layout: the ask first (Decision needed: with lettered options, one recommended, and where to answer), then Proposed direction: and Next:, only the tags bold. The work stays inside the row's Selected Sections; a row with none gets a question asking which, and any edit outside them is named on an Outside the selected sections: line. PRs are named as repo#n, which the sheet script links, and it adds a Where to review line linking each selected section on the preview. The agent then runs tools/review-log-watch/lint.ts and fixes what it flags: a cell that breaks the layout, or a PR state that GitHub contradicts. The agent records its step on the Agent tab at once, with the real time. Previews follow main: by default (Config PREVIEW_REFRESH automatic) the agent runs tools/review-log-watch/previews.ts on every poll for every open change-set PR, and also when people act on a change set (new Blue feedback, Ready for agent set to Yes, or feedback asking to update the preview); with PREVIEW_REFRESH on-feedback, only then. A branch behind main gets main merged in (a merge commit), pushed and restaged; a conflict a person must settle is asked in the change set's feedback.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-sheet-script"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>WF06</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>WF07</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:callActivity id="Task_RecordStep" name="Record agent step on each row it wrote" calledElement="Process_RecordAgentStep">
      <bpmn:documentation>For every row the pass or the stall check wrote, Record agent step: the Agent tab row first (status, pull request, preview, step), then Feedback (agent) from it, then read back Agentic status and Staging review. A row whose Feedback (agent) names a pull request or preview its Agent row does not, or whose Agent step is not "&lt;step&gt; &lt;time&gt;", is fixed here.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-sheet-agent-columns"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>WF07</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>WF10</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:callActivity>
    <bpmn:serviceTask id="Task_Accept" name="Accept the new state">
      <bpmn:documentation>Runs the check again with --accept, so the state file holds what was just handled and the next poll compares against it. A row the pass could not finish stays changed and is picked up on the next poll.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:extensionElements><bootstrap.processes:skill ref="review-log-watch"/></bpmn:extensionElements>
      <bpmn:incoming>WF10</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>WF08</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:serviceTask>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_Done" name="Changes handled">
      <bpmn:incoming>WF08</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="EndEvent_NoWork" name="Nothing changed">
      <bpmn:documentation>No agent work: the next wake is queued and the poll ends.</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>WF05</bpmn:incoming>
    </bpmn:endEvent>

    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="WF01" sourceRef="StartEvent_Poll" targetRef="Task_ReadSheet" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="WF02" sourceRef="Task_ReadSheet" targetRef="Task_RunCheck" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="WF03" sourceRef="Task_RunCheck" targetRef="Task_StallCheck" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="WF09" sourceRef="Task_StallCheck" targetRef="Gateway_Changed" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="WF04" name="changed" sourceRef="Gateway_Changed" targetRef="Task_AppendRows" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="WF05" name="unchanged" sourceRef="Gateway_Changed" targetRef="EndEvent_NoWork" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="WF06" sourceRef="Task_AppendRows" targetRef="Task_AgentPass" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="WF07" sourceRef="Task_AgentPass" targetRef="Task_RecordStep" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="WF10" sourceRef="Task_RecordStep" targetRef="Task_Accept" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="WF08" sourceRef="Task_Accept" targetRef="EndEvent_Done" />
  </bpmn:process>

  <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="BPMNDiagram_ReviewLogWatch">
    <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="BPMNPlane_1" bpmnElement="Collaboration_ReviewLogWatch">
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Participant_ReviewLogWatch_di" bpmnElement="Participant_ReviewLogWatch" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="160" y="60" width="1332" height="330" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Lane_Watcher_di" bpmnElement="Lane_Watcher" isHorizontal="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="190" y="60" width="1302" height="330" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="StartEvent_Poll_di" bpmnElement="StartEvent_Poll">
        <dc:Bounds x="220" y="137" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="180" y="179" width="116" height="30" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_ReadSheet_di" bpmnElement="Task_ReadSheet">
        <dc:Bounds x="316" y="110" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_RunCheck_di" bpmnElement="Task_RunCheck">
        <dc:Bounds x="496" y="110" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Gateway_Changed_di" bpmnElement="Gateway_Changed" isMarkerVisible="true">
        <dc:Bounds x="676" y="130" width="50" height="50" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="636" y="90" width="130" height="30" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_AppendRows_di" bpmnElement="Task_AppendRows">
        <dc:Bounds x="786" y="110" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_AgentPass_di" bpmnElement="Task_AgentPass">
        <dc:Bounds x="966" y="110" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_Accept_di" bpmnElement="Task_Accept">
        <dc:Bounds x="1146" y="110" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_Done_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_Done">
        <dc:Bounds x="1326" y="137" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="1286" y="179" width="116" height="30" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="EndEvent_NoWork_di" bpmnElement="EndEvent_NoWork">
        <dc:Bounds x="683" y="280" width="36" height="36" />
        <bpmndi:BPMNLabel><dc:Bounds x="643" y="322" width="116" height="30" /></bpmndi:BPMNLabel>
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="WF01_di" bpmnElement="WF01">
        <di:waypoint x="256" y="155" />
        <di:waypoint x="316" y="155" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="WF02_di" bpmnElement="WF02">
        <di:waypoint x="436" y="155" />
        <di:waypoint x="496" y="155" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_StallCheck_di" bpmnElement="Task_StallCheck">
        <dc:Bounds x="496" y="250" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="WF03_di" bpmnElement="WF03">
        <di:waypoint x="556" y="200" />
        <di:waypoint x="556" y="250" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="WF09_di" bpmnElement="WF09">
        <di:waypoint x="616" y="295" />
        <di:waypoint x="646" y="295" />
        <di:waypoint x="646" y="155" />
        <di:waypoint x="676" y="155" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="WF04_di" bpmnElement="WF04">
        <di:waypoint x="726" y="155" />
        <di:waypoint x="786" y="155" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="WF05_di" bpmnElement="WF05">
        <di:waypoint x="701" y="180" />
        <di:waypoint x="701" y="280" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="WF06_di" bpmnElement="WF06">
        <di:waypoint x="906" y="155" />
        <di:waypoint x="966" y="155" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="Task_RecordStep_di" bpmnElement="Task_RecordStep">
        <dc:Bounds x="1056" y="250" width="120" height="90" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNShape>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="WF07_di" bpmnElement="WF07">
        <di:waypoint x="1026" y="200" />
        <di:waypoint x="1026" y="295" />
        <di:waypoint x="1056" y="295" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="WF10_di" bpmnElement="WF10">
        <di:waypoint x="1176" y="295" />
        <di:waypoint x="1206" y="295" />
        <di:waypoint x="1206" y="200" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="WF08_di" bpmnElement="WF08">
        <di:waypoint x="1266" y="155" />
        <di:waypoint x="1326" y="155" />
      </bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
    </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
  </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
</bpmn:definitions>
